---
// Kairos seminar series with Dr. James Dyson, The Organic and Psychospiritual
// Basis of Mental Health, four Saturdays, September 26 - November 7, 2026.
// Copy is taken from the WordPress page it replaces:
// https://centerforanthroposophy.org/mental-health-from-an-anthroposophic-perspective-with-dr-james-dyson/
// (page 44886). The series was already running when it moved (2026-10-16);
// it sells the whole series at $350 as WordPress did. Kairos graduates arrive
// with ?coupon=GRADS25.
//
// The checkout lives in src/components/KairosDysonCheckout.astro. Left noindex
// (the site default).
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import KairosDysonCheckout from '../../components/KairosDysonCheckout.astro';

const seminars = [
  { label: 'Seminar One', title: 'Mysteries of Embodiment. Two Streams of Incarnation', date: 'Saturday, September 26, 2026', time: '3:00 – 5:00 PM EDT' },
  { label: 'Seminar Two', title: 'Attachment Dynamics and Personality Structure', date: 'Saturday, October 24, 2026', time: '3:00 – 5:00 PM EDT' },
  { label: 'Seminar Three', title: 'Organology. Planetary Qualities and the Ethers in Relation to the Threefold Nature of the Human Soul', date: 'Saturday, October 31, 2026', time: '3:00 – 5:00 PM EDT' },
  { label: 'Seminar Four', title: 'Developmental and Spiritual Challenges of our Times. Understanding the Separation of the Three Soul Forces and Encountering the Guardian of the Threshold', date: 'Saturday, November 7, 2026', time: '3:00 – 5:00 PM EST' },
];
---

<Base
  title="Register: The Organic and Psychospiritual Basis of Mental Health with Dr. James Dyson | Center for Anthroposophy"
  portalLabel={null}
  minimal
>
  <header class="registration-head">
    <div class="wrap registration-intro">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow series-link">Kairos Institute · Four online seminars</p>
        <h1>The Organic and Psychospiritual Basis of Mental Health</h1>
        <p class="cohort">with Dr. James Dyson</p>
        <p class="intro-copy">
          Four Saturday afternoons on the ground beneath mental health: how soul lives in relation
          to body and spirit, and what that means for anyone working with people in difficulty.
          Dr. Dyson has spent five decades in anthroposophic medicine, twenty-five of them in
          clinical practice at Park Attwood.
        </p>
        <p class="course-details">Four Saturdays, September 26 to November 7, 2026<br />
          3:00 – 5:00 PM Eastern</p>
        <p class="course-format">Online by Zoom · $350 for the series</p>
        <a class="course-link" href="#registration-form">See registration details <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="when-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">The four seminars</p>
        <ol class="seminar-list">
          {seminars.map((seminar) => (
            <li>
              <span class="seminar-no">{seminar.label}</span>
              <strong>{seminar.date}</strong>
              <span class="seminar-parts">{seminar.title}<br />{seminar.time}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
        <p class="when-note">Each seminar runs two hours. The fee of $350 covers all four.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="wrap facilitator-welcome" aria-labelledby="speaker-title">
    <img class="facilitator-photo" src="/images/74da18d95f-james-dyson.webp"
      alt="Portrait of Dr. James Dyson."
      width="150" height="150" loading="lazy" />
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Anthroposophic medicine · Psychosynthesis</p>
      <h2 id="speaker-title">James Dyson, M.D.</h2>
      <p>Dr. Dyson trained as a medical doctor at London University, then studied anthroposophic
        medicine at Emerson College, Camphill Schools Aberdeen, and in hospitals in Germany. In 1979
        he co-founded Park Attwood Clinic, a residential medical facility in the UK, where he
        practiced for twenty-five years. He has also worked as a school doctor, both in Waldorf
        schools and in schools and communities for adults and children with special needs.</p>
      <p>In 2008 he completed a five-year program in Applied Psychosynthesis at the Institute of
        Psychosynthesis, London, and was later awarded a master's degree in Psychosynthesis
        Psychology from Middlesex University.</p>
      <p>He has lectured for decades across international anthroposophic medical and therapeutic
        trainings, and contributes regularly to conferences of the Medical Section at the
        Goetheanum. As a founding faculty member of the Association for Anthroposophic Psychology
        in the USA in 2014, he remains a regular contributor to their foundation programs. His
        current practice takes in clinical mentoring and independent consulting.</p>
      <p>His work lies in connecting esoteric experience with cognitive understanding,
        particularly around psychosomatic medicine, mental health, and human relationship.
        <em>Soul Size: The Eternal Psychosomatic Dilemma</em>, published by SteinerBooks in 2022,
        collects his lectures, essays, and interviews on soul in relation to body and spirit.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap module-section" aria-labelledby="audience-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Who this is for</p>
    <h2 id="audience-title">For people who work with others</h2>
    <p>The seminars are pitched at people who already work with others: therapists, doctors,
      teachers, counselors, and those training toward that work. No prior study of anthroposophic
      medicine is assumed, though the material moves quickly for anyone entirely new to
      anthroposophy.</p>
    <p>The series is part of the Kairos Institute’s 2026–27 public offerings, which also include
      Emergency Pedagogy Module 7 with Bernd Ruf in January and the Bridge Lectures with Michaela
      Glöckler in the new year. Questions about the series can go to Lisl Hofer at
      <a href="mailto:lisl@centerforanthroposophy.org">lisl@centerforanthroposophy.org</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <KairosDysonCheckout />
</Base>

<style>
  .registration-head {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: linear-gradient(120deg, rgba(176, 136, 16, 0.12), transparent 62%);
    padding: 56px 0 48px;
  }
  .registration-intro {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(0, 0.8fr);
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .registration-head h1 {
    font-size: clamp(36px, 4.6vw, 58px);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    margin-top: 6px;
  }
  .series-link { color: var(--green-ink); }
  .cohort {
    color: var(--gold);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 18px;
    letter-spacing: 0.035em;
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  .intro-copy { color: var(--soft); font-size: 20px; max-width: 52ch; margin-top: 24px; }
  .course-details { font: 600 16px/1.7 var(--sans); margin-top: 24px; }
  .course-format { color: var(--soft); font: 14px/1.7 var(--sans); margin-top: 8px; }
  .course-link { display: inline-flex; gap: 16px; margin-top: 24px; color: var(--green-ink); font: 600 15px var(--sans); text-underline-offset: 5px; }
  .course-link:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--green); outline-offset: 6px; }
  .when-card { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 3px solid var(--gold); background: var(--raised); padding: 26px 28px; min-width: 0; }
  .seminar-list { list-style: none; margin: 14px 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  .seminar-list li { display: grid; gap: 2px; }
  .module-section { padding-top: 40px; padding-bottom: 40px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .module-section h2 { font-size: clamp(25px, 3vw, 34px); margin: 8px 0 16px; }
  .module-section p { max-width: 68ch; margin-top: 12px; }
  .seminar-no { color: var(--gold); font: 11px var(--sans); letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .seminar-list strong { font-size: 19px; font-weight: 600; }
  .seminar-parts { color: var(--soft); font: 14px/1.7 var(--sans); }
  .when-note { color: var(--soft); font: 13px/1.6 var(--sans); margin-top: 16px; }
  .facilitator-welcome { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 150px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 36px; align-items: start; padding-top: 48px; padding-bottom: 48px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .facilitator-photo { width: 150px; height: 150px; border-radius: 50%; object-fit: cover; }
  .facilitator-welcome h2 { font-size: clamp(25px, 3vw, 34px); margin: 8px 0 16px; }
  .facilitator-welcome p { max-width: 68ch; margin-top: 12px; }
  .welcome-credit { color: var(--soft); font: 14px/1.6 var(--sans); margin-top: 20px; }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .registration-intro { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 22px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .registration-head { padding: 38px 0 34px; }
    .facilitator-welcome { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 22px; padding-top: 32px; padding-bottom: 32px; }
    .facilitator-photo { width: 110px; height: 110px; }
  }
</style>
